VECTOR SOURCE AND INHERITED IMAGE MATERIALS

The Vector-derived component catalog/schema and bundled component artwork
originate from Vector v0.58.0, commit
2bcad9bbb84e201dcfd58c22b1f779290101b728, under MPL-2.0. Corresponding original
source: https://github.com/vectordotdev/vector/tree/v0.58.0
Immutable source: https://github.com/vectordotdev/vector/tree/2bcad9bbb84e201dcfd58c22b1f779290101b728
Vectory modifications and reproducible catalog inputs are available in
vector-catalog/ and dashboard/src/generated/ in the matching Vectory source
release: https://github.com/416rehman/Vectory/tree/v0.1.1
Individual component artwork source URLs and SHA-256 digests are retained in
dashboard/src/assets/component-icons/provenance.json and below. Names/logos
identify their respective services; no endorsement is asserted.

The validator container redistributes the pinned official Vector 0.58.0 binary.
It retains /usr/share/vector/NOTICE, /usr/share/vector/LICENSE-3rdparty.csv and
full upstream license texts under /usr/share/vector/licenses/. Its Vector
source is available at the immutable URL above. The container also retains
installed operating-system package copyright/license files under
/usr/share/doc/ and /usr/share/common-licenses/.

PAGEFIND COMPILED SEARCH AND CORRESPONDING SOURCE

Offline Help search uses precompiled Pagefind 1.5.2 WebAssembly. Its locked
normal dependency pagefind_microjson 0.1.4 supplies GPL-3.0-only code; that
compiled search component is accompanied by the full GPLv3 text below and a
local corresponding-source archive. This does not describe Vectory's own
Apache-2.0 source as GPL-only.
Download from the installed or public Help distribution:
/help/legal/pagefind-1.5.2-source.tar.gz
Provenance and archive/WASM hashes:
/help/legal/pagefind-1.5.2-source.json
The archive contains exact upstream source commit
a2e9f40ef326f9a7926247695df25981a6f3ef4b, all 22 locked WASM package sources,
their license texts, the Snowball 3.0.0 preferred algorithm/generator source,
and optional developer rebuild instructions. Ordinary
Vectory installation uses prebuilt kits and does not require a compiler.
Primary upstream source:
https://github.com/Pagefind/pagefind/tree/a2e9f40ef326f9a7926247695df25981a6f3ef4b

Instrument Sans is bundled with its full SIL Open Font License 1.1 and original
copyright statement below; font-specific copies remain in the fonts folders.

